  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water Technical Assistance Facility NDCP 2026-2030 work programme UNOPS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Water Technical Assistance Facility provides technical assistance and embedded advisory services to IGG priority countries focused on the water related implementation of NDCs 3.0. The activity is implemented by NDC Partnership in line with its 2026-2030 work programme which aims to enable developing countries, by strengthening capacity, to accelerate NDC Implementation (Impact Pathway 1), mobilize finance for NDCs (Impact Pathway 2) and strengthen ambition (Impact Pathway 3) of NDCs 4.0. As matchmaker NDCP supports developing countries in strengthening enabling conditions to advance climate action on the water-energy-food-climate nexus. The type of support NDCP can include:
- Development, coordination and monitoring of sectoral implementation plans aligned with NDCs;
- Support in mobilizing finance via the development of investment plans and pipeline development (i.e. pre-feasibility and concept note development) and connections with relevant financial actors (in the NDCP network);
- Strengthen the integration of climate, food and water in policy, budgets and regulatory frameworks;
- Strengthen institutional capacity of governments (i.e. inter-ministerial coordination and strengthened implementation via embedded advisors and in-country facilitators);
- NDC implementation via technical assistance.
The added value of this activity vis a vis the IGG portfolio is its contribution to the strengthening of the enabling environment and specifically building the capacity of relevant governments to advance the water related implementation of NDCs 3.0. The intended results are related to the enabling environment indicators of the IGG results framework for water.  The final results will also depend on the demand by countries and the prioritization of support by the Ministry in close consultations with embassies.</narrative>
  </description>
